WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.260
- On our show,

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.870
we want to put a spotlight
on people doing real good,

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.890
out in the real world.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.020
And as the wildfires continue
to affect the West Coast,

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.680
there are countless stories
of heroes risking their lives

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.250
to help save their neighbors.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.120
And our next guest is one of those heroes.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.310
Having saved countless lives
and countless other homes,

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.580
while losing her own home.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.710
Joining us from Oregon,

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.570
please welcome the Upper
McKenzie Rural Fire Chief,

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.344
Chief Christiana Rainbow Plews.

00:00:32.344 --> 00:00:34.490
(audience applause)

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.323
- Thank you.

00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:38.100
- Hello, Chief Rainbow.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.410
Oh, I'm so--
- Hi, thanks for having me.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.193
- I was just gonna say
thank you for coming here.

00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:44.200
( Chief Rainbow laughs)

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.660
Take us through everything.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.823
How has your community
been affected by the fires?

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.750
- The community is completely devastated,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.190
Blue River's gone.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.730
It's a small town in the
Cascade Foothills in Oregon

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.760
and it is completely gone.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.210
Not only all the homes
but all the businesses

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.943
including our fire station.

00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:10.478
- Oh! And--

00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:13.070
- Eight of my volunteer
firefighters have lost

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.210
all of their belongings and their homes.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.140
- And you lost your home,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.090
Right, Chief Rainbow?.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:20.970
- I did,

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.550
I did. I lost my home
and my neighboring home

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.910
where my boys were
roommates as also thought.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:30.650
- Oh! How have you dealt with this?

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.310
How have you been able to

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.520
handle everything that's been

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.890
you know, put on your plate

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.390
that you've been confronted with?

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.983
How are you coping?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.300
- It's really a roller coaster.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.510
I'm up and down,

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.310
one minute I feel like

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.420
I'm strong enough to handle all of it

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.700
and the next minute, I don't know,

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.380
really lost.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.120
I've been getting my
strength from my family,

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.770
and I know that my firefighters
are also gaining strength

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.690
from their families.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.323
And,

00:02:05.323 --> 00:02:06.413
our strong,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:10.930
partners all around us
in the fire community,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.050
are really supporting us.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.910
- Can I ask you a question
because watching this story,

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.320
I think of the person

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.230
in me that is here

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.880
watching a television in my kitchen.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.400
How do you tell yourself,
I've lost my home,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.020
my boys are struggling,

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:28.890
I'm struggling.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.540
What is the flip, the switch you flip

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.120
to go back out there
and keep helping others

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.670
while you're dealing with that?

00:02:38.806 --> 00:02:40.110
- Somebody has to do it.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:44.040
Somebody has to lead and
somebody has to help,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.820
get the healing

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.660
and the,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.690
rebuilding process started.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.210
And I am the chief

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.830
and I am in the position

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.950
to impact that.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.528
So, I just have to be strong

00:02:58.528 --> 00:03:00.290
and I have to do it

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.236
for everyone else.

00:03:02.236 --> 00:03:04.330
And hopefully, we can all find our way.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.870
- We would like to do something
for you, Chief Rainbow.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.470
I was so invested in your story

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.320
and we spoke to our friends at Pastene,

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.180
the oldest Italian specialty
foods in North America.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.070
And they were just incredible
and they responded,

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.130
and we wanted to give you

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.550
this $10,000 cheque

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.919
on behalf of them

00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:26.560
(audience applause)
and all of us at the show.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.480
And I know it's not enough,
(audience continues clapping)

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.180
but just a little start to say

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.990
that you are an inspiration to us all.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:39.130
And I'm going to be replaying
that in my mind over and over

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.680
that when you're in some
of the hardest situations,

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.960
how you flip that switch
and care for others.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.670
I have learned a lot from you.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.780
And I just thank you for your
dedication and inspiration

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.760
and talking with us today.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.070
So here's--
- That's too much

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.690
a little something not enough,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:00.620
but I thank our friends at Pastene,

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.430
and thank you Chief Rainbow for
being the example to us all.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.477
We'll be right back.
- Thank you so much Drew.

00:04:07.477 --> 00:04:09.430
Thank you. Thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:13.347
(high intensity techno music)

